A||||6||Songman||Question about SEs||||1||
Z||000000||Songman||04-05-2001||12:17 AM||||I have been seeing this little red Fiero running around close by my house. Today he pulled out about a half mile ahead of me going down the road. I could tell it was an older gentleman driving. I decided to follow him and invite him to participate in our activites (should we ever actually have any activities).<P>Here's the question... As I was following him I noticed that the trunk sticker said 2M4. But then I noticed the double outlet dual exhaust and GT style rear bumper cover, bubble type decklid, etc... I knew it was a later model car... When he finally stopped and I talked to him, he told me that he had bought the car new in 86 and it is a totally original SE. I thought later SEs all had V6s in them. Obviously, this is incorrect. Anybody got numbers?<P>This guy loves his little car. It has been repainted and looks great. Turns out that he is a Baptist preacher at a little church down the road! This is his daily driver and sometime weekend fun car. He also has an MG-TD kit car...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||04-05-2001||12:22 AM||||84 SE 4-cyl (Obviously)<BR>85 thru 87 SE 4-cyl standard/ V-6 optional.<BR>86/87 had aero notchback. 85 SE had base coupe body.<P>I don't know production #'s<P>I have only seen very few (maybe 6 total) 86/87 SE's with the 4-cyl.<P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||04-05-2001||12:22 AM||||SE's always came stock with the 4 banger.  85-87 the 6 was an option.  All 86-87 SE's got the aero styling and dual exhaust.<P>Jinx!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 04-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||04-05-2001||12:25 AM||||Excellent work, Songman!<BR>Bring in the lost sheep.<BR>Even if you have to chase em down.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||6
Z||000004||Songman||04-05-2001||12:31 AM||||You guys are quick! Thanks for clearing that up. <P>I'll get em Cheever! I'll probably end up scaring someone to death one of these days and probably get arrested! Some people might get a little paranoid with some long haired guy following them around! heheh<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Kelvin Vivian||04-05-2001||02:27 AM||||Songman,<P>Here are the production numbers of 86 & 87 SEs which have the aero GT front end and dual exhausts, what I like is that even the 4-cyl SEs come with the dual exhaust. <P>86 SE 4-cyl: 4,031<BR>86 SE V6: 28,274<P>87 SE 4-cyl: 1,401<BR>87 SE V6: 2,474<P>The car you saw was 1 of 4,031 86 SE 2M4s.  In 1987, the designation of 2M4/2M6 was dropped, the back of my 1987 SE just says "Fiero".  You'd have to open the rear decklid (or perhaps judge the width of the tires on the rims) to see if its a 4-cyl or a V6.<P>Kelvin<BR>88 GT T-top, 5-spd<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||04-05-2001||03:03 AM||||Wow! Thanks Kelvin... The preacher man will be glad to know he has sort of a rare car! He said he doesn't know anything about it really.. he just thinks it is fun to drive! heheh<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
